  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Electron releasing substituent like <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> increase the basicity of amines by dispersing positive charge of the anilium ion. However, their presence at ortho position decreases the basicity due to ortho effect. <br/>Thus, <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/c0cbb030-8312-47c8-9124-9ffba6208cc9.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.30833in;height:1.19167in\"> is most basic and compound Y is least basic.",
